ey: string, path: string, ttlMs = 30_000): Promise<T> {\n  const cached = cacheGet<{ t: number; v: T } | null>(key, null);\n  if (cached && Date.now() - cached.t < ttlMs) return cached.v;\n  const fresh = await request<T>(path);\n  cacheSet(key, { t: Date.now(), v: fresh });\n  return fresh;\n}\n```\n\nGood candidates: `phrases()`, `outcomes()`, `languageSettings()`, `platformSettings()` — these change rarely but are likely re-fetched on every navigation to Library/Settings.\n\n## 4. Memory leaks\n\n**`useCountUp.ts`** — `requestAnimationFrame` loop has no cancellation. If `target` changes mid-animation or the component unmounts, the old `tick` recursion keeps running and calls `setValue`/touches `ref.current` after unmount.\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (target === 0) { setValue(0); return; }\n  let cancelled = false;\n  let rafId: number;\n  const start = performance.now();\n  ref.current?.classList.add('counting');\n  const tick = (now: number) => {\n    if (cancelled) return;\n    const progress = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);\n    const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\n    setValue(Math.round(target * eased));\n    if (progress < 1) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    else ref.current?.classList.remove('counting');\n  };\n  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  return () => { cancelled = true; cancelAnimationFrame(rafId); };\n}, [target, duration]);\n```\n\n**`useToasts.ts`** timers — see above, same leak class.\n\n## 5. Redundant computations\n\n**`utils/transcript.ts`** — `buildConversationItems` runs `.filter()` over `events` and `.map()`/`.sort()` over turns on every call; if this is invoked from a render path with the same `transcript`/`events` reference, wrap the call site in `useMemo` keyed on `transcript._id` and `events.length`.\n\n**`OUTCOME_CATEGORIES`/`DEFAULT_OUTCOME_RULES`** (`constants/outcomes.ts`) are module-level constants — fine as-is, not recomputed. No action needed.\n\n**`parseApiDate`** (`utils/formatting.ts`) — regex-tests every call; called repeatedly per transcript turn in `buildConversationItems`. Low cost individually but on large transcripts (hundreds of turns) this is O(n) regex work per render. If `TranscriptsView` re-renders often, memoizing the conversation-items array (above) eliminates this too.\n\n---\n\n### Priority order\n1. **`useCountUp` RAF leak** — real bug, fix now (small diff, clear correctness win).\n2. **`useToasts` timer cleanup** — real leak, small fix.\n3. **Cache layer for read-heavy GETs** (phrases/outcomes/settings) — biggest perceived-speed win, `cache.ts` infrastructure already exists.\n4. **Memoize `buildConversationItems` call sites** in transcript views.\n\nWant me to apply the `useCountUp` and `useToasts` fixes directly, since those are clear bugs with no tradeoffs?\n",
